Tadayoshi became a priest and retired from politics, but there is a theory that Tadayoshi had an agreement between Moronao and Takauji and actively intended to resign from the position of his master.
Takauji appointed his legitimate son Yoshiakira from Kamakura to control the government, instead of Tadayoshi, and instead, he appointed his second son Motouji ASHIKAGA as Kamakura kubo, and established Kamakura Prefecture to govern the eastern provinces.
After Tadayoshi retired from the position of Tadayoshi, Tadafuyu ASHIKAGA, an illegitimate child and adopted child of Tadayoshi, expanded his power as Tadayoshi's side in Kyushu, and Takauji went to the Chugoku region to subjugate Tadafuyu in 1350.
